        <solution>
            <p>
        Problem 3: the polynomial is: <m>P(x) = 0.12 + 0.2(x-0.1) - 1.5(x-0.1)(x-0.2) + 10(x-0.1)(x-0.2)(x-0.3)</m> for part b) if you add the data point (0.5,0.11) then the next term in the polynomial is: <md>-6.25(x-0.1)(x-0.2)(x-0.3)(x-0.4)</md> </p> 
<p> Problem 4: The polynomial is: <md> P(x) = 2 + 0(x-1)-1(x-1)(x-2)+\frac 23(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)</md> </p>
<p> Problem 5: The polynomial is: 
    <md> P(x) = 10 + 1.6(x-10)-0.0016(x-10(x-30)</md>
    </p>
<p> Problem 6: The polynomial is: 
<md> P(x)=0.987-0.925(x-1) + 0.8094 (x-1)(x-2.2)</md></p>
        </solution>
